<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="probe-engine-core" data-rev="0">
  <!-- @include-skip files-touched rows and callouts follow the sibling plan fragments' inline markup so the page renders them identically -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/cli.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Five short-help strings that exceed 80 columns under -h are shortened, and the detail moves to the long help. resume --json states that the extension is replaced by .jsonl, as simulate --json already does.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/src</td><td>+14 / -6</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine-cli/tests/cli_args.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The 80-column test reads -h and --help on all 8 help surfaces. New regression tests cover the dump path, one OS-error mention, and no escape byte on redirected stderr. After Q-1: three failure-record tests.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/tests</td><td>+150 / -6</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/observe/mod.rs (awaiting Q-1)</summary><div class="pl-card">FailureRecord carries the envelope, outcome error, and error.type, error.code, and error.retriable, and no statistic key. EngineError::classify() maps each variant to the error keys.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src/observe</td><td>+60</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/main.rs, bench.rs (awaiting Q-1)</summary><div class="pl-card">When simulate or bench fails, the command prints one failure record on stdout, then the prose line on stderr, and exits 1. The bench --matches check returns a typed configuration error.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/src</td><td>+32 / -4</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> README.md (awaiting Q-1)</summary><div class="pl-card">The simulate and bench sections state that a failed run prints one record with outcome error and exits 1.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>README.md</td><td>+4</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Q-1 is a contract decision (high).</strong> Finding 2 has two remedies: emit a failure record, or narrow the outcome values in the contract. The plan stops at awaiting-input and recommends option A. Option A implements the confirmed error keys and changes no persisted file.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Outcome value drift (medium).</strong> The calibration plan writes outcome "failure", but the contract lists success, error, and abandoned. This plan uses error, and the calibration plan must align before it is implemented.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Help text regression (low).</strong> Short help puts each description on the option line. The widened test fails the gate if a later option makes a line longer than 80 columns.</aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>0 prior revisions</summary><ul></ul></details>
